(Every October, when the Atlantic fog rolled across the granite jetty) Tj T*
(of Saltgate, the town retreated indoors by five o'clock. Shopkeepers) Tj T*
(drew iron shutters, trawlers groaned against rubber fenders, and the) Tj T*
(salt wind rattled the leaded windows of the university reading room.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Clara Lindholm, a second-year literature student clutching a soaked) Tj T*
(notebook, paused at the end of the cobbled lane. Beyond the iron gate,) Tj T*
(the breakwater stretched into grey water like a sleeping spine.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Halfway down the pier stood a small warm diamond of amber light.) Tj T*
(It did not sweep in rhythmic circles like the tall white lighthouse on) Tj T*
(the headland; it hung steadily beside a rusted iron ring, swaying only) Tj T*
(when a gust shouldered against the wall.) Tj T*
