(Curiosity outran the cold. Clara pulled her wool coat tighter and) Tj T*
(walked out along the slick flagstones until she reached the lantern.) Tj T*
(Its glass panes were freshly wiped, and inside, a neat wick burned) Tj T*
(with smokeless clarity.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Crouching beside the low parapet sat an older man in a faded navy) Tj T*
(oilskin, adjusting a small copper oil can. His boots were scarred with) Tj T*
(dried brine, and his hands moved with the unhurried certainty of) Tj T*
(someone who had performed the same task for thirty winters.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
('The main beacon on North Point has three thousand watts,' Clara) Tj T*
(said gently, gesturing toward the distant beam slicing the fog.) Tj T*
('Why hang an oil lamp down here where only gulls can see it?') Tj T*
