(Clara looked back toward the town. From the pier, the streetlights) Tj T*
(were blurred haloes behind wet glass, and the high lighthouse beam) Tj T*
(swept silently overhead without touching the dark pocket of water) Tj T*
(below the seawall.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(She thought of the essays she had written all semester about grand) Tj T*
(metaphors and towering symbols, while overlooking quiet precision.) Tj T*
(Opening her damp notebook, she sheltered the paper beneath her coat) Tj T*
(and wrote a single line across the top of a blank page:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
('Not every signal is meant for the horizon; some lights exist only) Tj T*
(to guide the weary safely to the final step.') Tj T*
