(Out in the channel, an oarlock clinked softly against timber. Two) Tj T*
(young fishermen emerged from the grey curtain, steering their dory) Tj T*
(straight toward the amber glow beside the iron ring.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The harbour-keeper raised two fingers in quiet acknowledgement as) Tj T*
(the bow nudged the old tyres along the stone steps. Neither boatman) Tj T*
(needed to speak; the lantern had already answered their unspoken) Tj T*
(question before they left the mussel beds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
